# Dev-mode env (COMMITTED — shared convention). Loaded ONLY by `electron-vite dev`
# (Vite mode=development), and it wins over the gitignored `.env`/`.env.local`.
# A production build does NOT load this file, so staging/prod defaults still apply.
#
# GOAL: in `pnpm dev`, EVERYTHING our-side hits LOCAL services (localhost) — backend,
# admin, cloud redaction, AND auth. These VITE_* overrides win over the baked table in
# dev mode only, so the `OPENMASQ_BILLING` gate below does not apply here — the local
# stack is yours. Bring it up first:
#   cd apps/backend && docker compose up -d      # Postgres + GoTrue(:8000) + gateway + Mailpit(:8025)
#   pnpm --filter @openmasq/backend migrate && … seed && … dev:bootstrap  # schema + catalog + dev user
#   pnpm --filter @openmasq/backend dev         # → :3003
#   pnpm --filter @openmasq/redact-fn dev       # → :8080 (SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 + GPTOSS_API_KEY)
#   pnpm --filter @openmasq/web dev             # → :4400 (admin console)
# The renderer CSP (dev-only Vite plugin) allows http://localhost:* only in dev mode.
#
# ⚠️ Fully-local sign-in needs the docker stack running: auth now targets the LOCAL
# GoTrue (:8000). Use the dev:bootstrap account (dev@local.openmasq / devpassword123);
# magic-link emails land in Mailpit (http://localhost:8025), and GoTrue's
# GOTRUE_URI_ALLOW_LIST must include `<protocol>://auth/callback` (the deep-link
# scheme from packages/branding) for the redirect to
# return. Don't want to run the stack? A personal `.env.development.local` (highest
# Vite precedence) can point VITE_SUPABASE_URL back at cloud Supabase.

# Remote backend (accounts / settings-sync / org-admin) — local backend.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3003
VITE_ADMIN_URL=http://localhost:4400/admin

# Account auth — LOCAL GoTrue behind the nginx gateway (:8000), same as apps/web's
# dev config. The bare GoTrue+gateway stack doesn't validate the anon key, so a
# placeholder matches (mirrors apps/web/.env.local NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY).
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=local-anon-key-placeholder

# Cloud redaction engine — local redact-fn on :8080. It verifies the Supabase JWT
# (no local bypass); with auth on local GoTrue above, start redact-fn with
# SUPABASE_URL=http://localhost:8000 + GPTOSS_API_KEY so its JWKS matches.
VITE_REDACT_FN_URL=http://localhost:8080

# Analytics relay (apps/analytics-fn) — forwards the sanitised analytics/$exception
# envelope to PostHog and proxies Contentful release notes. There is NO default: unset,
# the sink is a no-op and Settings → Versions shows no release notes (`appEnv.ts`).
# ⚠️ Analytics DEFAULTS ON in dev (consent `?? true`), so the sink emits and `debug`
# mode logs EVERY event to the console (env + version stamped, HMAC computed if a key is
# set) — that is the pipeline you can watch without any backend. To actually LAND dev
# events, run the relay locally (`pnpm --filter @openmasq/analytics-fn dev` → :8095,
# ANALYTICS_APP_KEYS unset ⇒ it accepts) and set this to http://localhost:8095/e, with a
# dev VITE_ANALYTICS_APP_KEY in a gitignored .env.development.local if your relay attests
# builds (events carry env:"development" — filter on it).

# The Versions tab lists releases from `VITE_UPDATES_CHANNEL` (baked via
# electron.vite.config.ts `define`, read from the SHELL env at build/dev-launch — NOT
# from this .env file). A dev build defaults to `desktop-production`, which has 0
# published builds, so the history shows only the running build. To see the real
# version history (dozens of `-staging.N` builds) + the infinite scroll, LAUNCH dev with
# the shell var:  VITE_UPDATES_CHANNEL=desktop-staging pnpm dev
# (dev-only cosmetic: real update checks are packaged-only, so this only changes which
# `/releases` list is displayed).

# ── YOUR OWN infrastructure — NOTHING here is committed (public repository) ────────────
# Supply these at BUILD time (CI or shell) to switch each capability ON. Unset ⇒ the
# capability is cleanly absent: no accounts and no sign-in gate, no backend (so no
# billing, sync, organizations or feedback), no gateway (so no server-side redaction and
# no platform-served models), no telemetry, no auto-update, OAuth connectors "not
# configured" — and the app runs entirely on the machine. Full runbook: SELF_HOSTING.md.
#   OPENMASQ_SUPABASE_URL=              # https://<ref>.supabase.co — accounts / auth
#   OPENMASQ_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=  # sb_publishable_…
#   OPENMASQ_BILLING=1                  # THE gate: without it the four addresses below are
#                                       # baked EMPTY even if supplied, and nothing is sold
#                                       # (scripts/buildDefines.ts). Auth, Slack relay,
#                                       # analytics and updates are NOT behind it.
#   OPENMASQ_BACKEND_URL=               # the API (billing, sync, organizations, feedback)
#   OPENMASQ_BACKEND_URL_STAGING=       # same, for a second environment (optional)
#   OPENMASQ_GATEWAY_URL=               # server-side redaction + platform-served models
#   OPENMASQ_GATEWAY_URL_STAGING=       # same, for a second environment (optional)
#   OPENMASQ_AUTH_URL=                  # the apps/auth relay (Slack connector only)
#   VITE_UPDATES_URL=                   # the apps/updates feed; unset ⇒ no auto-update
#   OPENMASQ_SENTRY_DSN=                # crash reports (main process)
#   OPENMASQ_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=          # GitHub connector (device flow)
#   OPENMASQ_SLACK_CLIENT_ID=           # Slack connector (with OPENMASQ_AUTH_URL)
#   OPENMASQ_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=          # Google connector ("Desktop app" client, PKCE)
#   OPENMASQ_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=      # same — non-confidential for a Desktop client
#   OPENMASQ_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=       # Microsoft connector (multi-tenant)
#   OPENMASQ_POSTHOG_KEY=               # analytics web (@openmasq/analytics, sites)
